      "id": "lpic1-package-source-selection",
      "version": 1,
      "track": "LPIC-1",
      "topic": "Debian source configuration",
      "unit": "debian-source-metadata",
      "title": "Choose Debian sources without losing updates",
      "summary": "Edit source targets, preserve the update source, and verify package availability without installing software.",
      "objective": "Select studio/main and studio/tools, retain studio-updates/main, and retire archive/main. Keep only these three required targets. Refresh the selected metadata so desk-viewer 1.4-2 is visible from studio/main, desk-indexer 2.1-1 from studio/tools, and base-security 1.1-1 from studio-updates/main. No package installation is needed.",
      "difficulty": "Beginner",
      "minutes": 20,
      "prerequisites": [
        "lpic1-package-file-provider"
      ],
      "retry_guidance": "Read each unmet requirement and the source\u2019s actual cache state. Correct the editor, Save sources, refresh when needed, and check again. Reset affects only this attempt; other work is retained.",
      "steps": [
        "Understand the selected targets.",
        "Save and refresh metadata deliberately.",
        "Inspect package provenance and check work."
      ],
      "guide": [],
      "hints": [
        "Compare each URI/suite/component target with the task requirements. One stanza selects every combination of its values.",
        "Saving does not fetch. Read Missing, Current and Retained matching cache separately.",
        "Use the exact package name and read its source/version; a same-named package from a retired target does not meet this task."
      ],
      "explanation": "A deb822 stanza selects the product of its URIs, Suites and Components. Keep the updates suite separate so only its main component is selected. Saving fixes selection; only refreshing supplies the new lists. Query evidence must come from the required selected source, not the retired archive or an unselected cache.",
      "sources": [
        "https://manpages.debian.org/trixie/apt/sources.list.5.en.html",
        "https://manpages.debian.org/trixie/apt/apt-get.8.en.html",
        "https://www.lpi.org/our-certifications/exam-101-102-objectives/"
      ],
      "simplifications": "Only the supplied deb822 selection excerpt and fixed offline publication snapshots are modeled; this is not a full secure .sources file. Other fields, trust/key/signature policy, real acquisition, APT policy/solver, installation and host files/commands are unsupported. Native Save, Refresh and Look up are simulator actions; the data-only internal reference is not a Linux command. This narrow source-selection/metadata practice does not complete objective 102.4 or prove real APT runtime conformance.",
